  "id": "Compound::DB00549 - Gene::1557",
  "verbalization": "Zafirlukast is shown to interact with Cyp2c19 through a series of interconnected pathways involving cytochrome P450 enzymes. The evidence suggests that Zafirlukast binds to Cyp2c8, which then participates in the metabolism of arachidonic acid, a key step in the production of pro-inflammatory mediators. This metabolic activity is also recognized by Cyp2c19, indicating a potential functional link between these enzymes. The shared participation in arachidonic acid monooxygenase activity by Cyp2c8 and Cyp2c19 implies that both enzymes may contribute to the same biological process, possibly in the context of lipid metabolism or inflammatory responses. The presence of multiple pathways connecting Zafirlukast to Cyp2c19 suggests a broader role for these enzymes in the metabolic regulation of arachidonic acid, potentially influencing inflammatory pathways. The integration of these findings highlights the importance of Cyp2c19 in the metabolic processing of arachidonic acid, with Zafirlukast possibly modulating this process through its interaction with Cyp2c8.",
